  "panels": [
    {
      "description": "",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {},
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 10,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "### SWIFT Networking\n\nUser-journey health for SWIFT-attached management cluster networking: shared control-plane router capacity and the Konnectivity tunnel/data path.\n\n**Sections:**\n- **Router / NIC Assignment** \u2014 management-cluster router-capacity SLO, per-HCP Pending-age evidence, and shared CNS pending-IP-programming state.\n- **NIC Capacity and CNS DaemonSet** \u2014 management-cluster/node health for the shared SWIFT NIC-assignment infrastructure.\n- **Konnectivity Tunnel** \u2014 per-HCP control-stream errors, dial-failure frequency, and packet volume for diagnosis.\n\n**Filters:**\n- Select a management cluster to scope every panel.\n- Optionally select one or more HCP namespaces to narrow the per-HCP Router and Konnectivity panels. Shared CNS and NIC-capacity panels remain management-cluster/node scoped because their telemetry has no HCP identity.\n\n**Datasources:**\n- Router and Konnectivity panels use the **HCP AMW** (`Managed_Prometheus_hcps-*`).\n- CNS and NIC-capacity panels use the **services AMW** (`Managed_Prometheus_services-*`).\n\n**Usage:** start with [SWIFT TSG: Establish Blast Radius](https://aka.ms/arohcp-tsg-swift#step-1-establish-blast-radius) to establish management-cluster scope, then use the HCP Pending-age and Konnectivity panels to isolate the affected layer and tenants.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.6.9",
      "title": "Dashboard Info",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 10
      },
      "id": 2,
      "panels": [],
      "title": "Router / NIC Assignment",
      "type": "row"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource_hcp}"
      },
      "description": "p99 age of router pods that are currently Pending. This is per-HCP diagnostic evidence for a router missing the 300-second startup allowance, not the primary control-plane SLO input. No series means no router pods are currently Pending.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "pointSize": 5,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false
          },
          "unit": "s"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 11
      },
      "id": 3,
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": ["lastNotNull", "max"],
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.6.9",
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource_hcp}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "router:startup_latency:p99{cluster=~\"$cluster\", namespace=~\"$hcp_namespace\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{namespace}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Router Pending Age p99 (by HCP namespace)",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource_hcp}"
      },
      "description": "Primary SWIFT control-plane SLI: available router replicas divided by expected router replicas across all HCP namespaces on the selected management cluster. The SLO target is 99.95% over 28 days; alerts wait 300 seconds before notifying about a capacity shortfall.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "max": 1,
          "min": 0,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 0.9995
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "percentunit"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 11
      },
      "id": 18,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": ["lastNotNull"],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "value_and_name"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.6.9",
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource_hcp}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "swift_router_replicas:available{cluster=~\"$cluster\"} / swift_router_replicas:configured{cluster=~\"$cluster\"}",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false,
          "legendFormat": "Router capacity",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "SWIFT Router Capacity Availability",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource_hcp}"
      },
      "description": "Count of selected HCP namespaces with a router Pending for longer than the 300-second startup allowance. This supports control-plane SLO triage.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "none",
          "decimals": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 11
      },
      "id": 4,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": ["lastNotNull"],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "value_and_name"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.6.9",
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource_hcp}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "count(router:startup_latency:p99{cluster=~\"$cluster\", namespace=~\"$hcp_namespace\"} > 300) or vector(0)",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false,
          "legendFormat": "HCPs affected",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "HCPs With Router Pods Stuck > 300s",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource_hcp}"
      },
      "description": "Remaining error budget for the accepted 99.95% management-cluster router-capacity SLO over its rolling 28-day window. 100% means no eligible noncompliant intervals in the window; 0% means the budget is exhausted. For a newly eligible management cluster, this shows the budget consumed by the available portion of the 28-day window.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "decimals": 1,
          "max": 100,
          "min": 0,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 25
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 50
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "percent"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 19
      },
      "id": 20,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": ["lastNotNull"],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "value_and_name"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.6.9",
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource_hcp}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "clamp_min(((sum_over_time(swift_router_replicas:available{cluster=~\"$cluster\"}[28d]) / sum_over_time(swift_router_replicas:configured{cluster=~\"$cluster\"}[28d])) - 0.9995) / (1 - 0.9995) * 100, 0)",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false,
          "legendFormat": "Router-capacity error budget remaining",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "SWIFT Router-Capacity Error Budget Remaining (28d)",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource_hcp}"
      },
      "description": "Management-cluster router-capacity availability over time. The 99.95% target line is the accepted 28-day router-capacity SLO. This measures Kubernetes router capacity, not direct SWIFT NIC or data-path usability.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "pointSize": 5,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "thresholdsStyle": {
              "mode": "line"
            }
          },
          "max": 100,
          "min": 0,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 99.95
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "percent"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 18,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 19
      },
      "id": 21,
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": ["lastNotNull", "min"],
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.6.9",
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource_hcp}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "swift_router_replicas:available{cluster=~\"$cluster\"} / swift_router_replicas:configured{cluster=~\"$cluster\"} * 100",
          "legendFormat": "{{cluster}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "SWIFT Router Capacity Availability Over Time (SLO: 99.95% / 28d)",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource_svc}"
      },
      "description": "Reserved IPs that have not completed secondary-NIC attachment. One series per CNS pod (management cluster worker node). A non-zero value can be normal during concurrent provisioning; investigate only when sustained and correlated with router startup latency, MTPNC state, or CNS logs.",
